        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-12-07T18:06:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This ruling feels like the most applicable from Fireside chats.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Fireside Chats\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Fireside Chats:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<br>\nIf a card with a “you may use an additional power this turn” effect is played outside of your turn, or on your turn after the power phase, you immediately use a power (or skip). If it’s played on your turn before the power phase, you must wait until the power phase to use it.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It certainly makes it seem like you should get the power use immediately off Overdrive based on the scenario described as the power phase has already passed. &nbsp;</p>",
